---
_type: PltConcept
_label: 'Transitive'
journey: fref("/01-programming-language-theory/index.td")
status: 'mastered'
tags:
  - 'set theory & relation'
---

A property of a ${fref("/01-programming-language-theory/02-concepts/binary-relation.td")} $R$ on a set $T$ such that if $t_0\ R\ t_1$ and $t_1\ R\ t_2$ then $t_0\ R\ t_2$, for every $t_0$, $t_1$, $t_2$ $\in T$.
